<title>USA: Epitope reschedules annual meeting.</title>
<headline>Epitope reschedules annual meeting.</headline>
<dateline>BEAVERTON, Ore. 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Epitope Inc said it rescheduled its annual meeting of shareholders to June 17.</p>
<p>The meeting was originally set for April 29.</p>
<p>&quot;The adjournment is necessary due to recent developments at Andrew and Williamson Sales Co (A&amp;W) which Epitope acquired on December 12, 1997 in a merger transaction, and Epitope's resultant suit to rescind the A&amp;W transactions,&quot; said Adolph Ferro, chief executive officer of Epitope.</p>
<p>Earlier this month, thousands of schoolchildren were exposed to tainted strawberries, packaged by A&amp;W, that caused an outbreak of hepatitis A virus in at least 175 cases.</p>
</text>
